# OpenCode Hierarchical Multi-Agent Architecture

A strict **hierarchical multi-agent architecture** for OpenCode. Reasoning and
execution are separated: a read-only **Primary Orchestrator** plans and
supervises, eight read-only **Static Specialized Advisors** provide domain
analysis, and short-lived **Ephemeral Dynamic Workers** are the only roles that
write files or run shell commands.

The governing document is [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) in the repository root. It is
the constitution for every agent in this environment and is loaded automatically
by OpenCode as project instructions.

## Architecture

```text
[User Request]
      │
      ▼
Primary Orchestrator (`orchestrator`) — planning, supervision, user liaison
  ├── 8 Static Specialized Advisors — read-only analysis and directives
  │     project-plan-agent · clean-code-agent · security-agent · testing-agent
  │     correction-agent · git-agent · seo-agent · verification-agent
  └── Ephemeral Dynamic Workers (`ephemeral-worker`) — the ONLY writers/executors
        spawned per atomic task → execute → report (SUCCESS/FAILURE) → terminate
```

## Permission matrix

| Role | Read / Search | Spawn / Delegate | File Write & Diff | Terminal / Shell |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Primary Orchestrator** | ✅ Allowed | ✅ Allowed | ❌ **STRICTLY BLOCKED** | ❌ **STRICTLY BLOCKED** |
| **Static Specialized Advisors (8)** | ✅ Allowed | ❌ Blocked | ❌ **STRICTLY BLOCKED** | ❌ **STRICTLY BLOCKED** |
| **Ephemeral Dynamic Workers** | ✅ Allowed | ❌ Blocked | ✅ **FULL ACCESS** | ✅ **FULL ACCESS** |

The matrix is enforced in [`.opencode/opencode.json`](.opencode/opencode.json),
not merely instructed:

- `orchestrator` — `edit` and `shell` denied; `subagent` denied except an
  allowlist of the 8 advisors and `ephemeral-worker`.
- The 8 advisors — `edit`, `shell`, and `subagent` denied.
- `ephemeral-worker` — `edit` and `shell` allowed; `subagent` denied
  (Sub-subagent Prohibition).
- The `skill` permission action is denied for every agent: **this project ships
  no skills** and loads none.

Any denied invocation fails with the guardrail error from `AGENTS.md` §5:
`"Permission Denied: Agent role is restricted to Read-Only planning & analysis."`

## Core operating principles

1. **Separation of reasoning and execution** — orchestrator and advisors never
   touch the disk or terminal; workers do nothing else.
2. **Explicit Todo Lists** — the orchestrator and every subagent maintain an
   explicit `[ ]` / `[x]` list in reasoning and reports.
3. **Mandatory Clarification Gate** — any ambiguity stops the pipeline until the
   user clarifies. No silent assumptions, no invented defaults.

## Repository layout

```text
AGENTS.md                       # architecture specification (constitution)
README.md
docs/
  GITHUB_OPERATIONS_WORKFLOW.md # Git/GitHub flow through git-agent + workers
tools/
  jev/
    jev-evaluate.mjs            # advisory Jev (TypeSafe System One) evaluator
    README.md                   # Jev contract and configuration
.opencode/
  opencode.json                 # agents, permissions, command and plugins
```

There is intentionally no `.opencode/skills/` directory and no `SKILL.md`
anywhere in this project.

## Usage

Start a session (the default agent is `orchestrator`) with a natural-language
request, or use the entry-gate command:

```text
/Agent Implement this feature. Consult the advisors, delegate execution to
ephemeral workers, and return a concise outcome with verification evidence.
```

Arabic example:

> نفّذ هذه المهمة وفق معمارية الوكلاء المتعددة: خطّط، استشر المستشارين
> المختصين، وفوّض التنفيذ للعمال المؤقتين فقط، ثم أعد تقريرًا مختصرًا مع أدلة
> التحقق. إذا كان أي متطلب غامضًا فاسألني قبل المتابعة.

The orchestrator proposes the plan, consults advisors where needed, dispatches
atomic worker briefs, runs verification (with `correction-agent` and
`verification-agent` on failure/final review), and presents the outcome. Git and
GitHub side effects remain user-approved per action class — see
[docs/GITHUB_OPERATIONS_WORKFLOW.md](docs/GITHUB_OPERATIONS_WORKFLOW.md).

## Activation

1. Place `AGENTS.md` at the project root (done in this repository) or adapt it
   per project.
2. Keep `.opencode/opencode.json` in place; no skills are required or loaded.
3. Quit and restart OpenCode — existing sessions keep their previously loaded
   configuration, so only fresh sessions enforce the new permission matrix.

Validate the effective configuration at any time:

```powershell
opencode debug config
```
